     "<div dir=\"ltr\">blavaan 0.2-3 has been released; see <a href=\"http://faculty.missouri.edu/~merklee/blavaan/version.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://faculty.missouri.edu/~merklee/blavaan/version.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463742199000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2UA82Vsba_IePGDkt1ZBZh\">here</a> for more detail.<br><br>lavaan 0.5-23.1097 was coincidentally released on the same day, causing a bug in blavaan&#39;s coef() function. Until a fix is made, the workaround is<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">coef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;lavaan&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>where fit is an object of class blavaan.<br><br>Ed<br></div>"
    ]
